hooters  that were oddly absent from halo games  in the past abs was now available for  every gun  and armored abilities were replaced with  spartan abilities which involved using  thrusters to move in any direction  you could use the thrusters in different  ways for example you could quickly  perform a side dash and gain leverage  against an enemy  meanwhile using that same thruster while  sprinting at full speed would trigger a  shoulder bash  and even crouching while in a full  sprint would perform a slide  the first we'd seen in the series in  halo 5 you could command and give out  instructions to your ai squad  and unlike in previous games they would  stick around for the entire game  if playing with friends in co-op the  squad mates would take the role of the  ai squad  which meant different gameplay  experiences since each character had  different starting weapons  and even visual head changes similar to  halo 2's arbiter  spartan lock was a playable character  opposite of master chief  despite the co-op's support halo 5 only  allowed players to join together through  xbox live  with split screen becoming a thing of  the past the lack of local play extended  to halo 5's multiplayer as well  however halo 5 made several changes to  improve upon the missteps of halo 4.  the arena-style combat was back with the  removal of weapon loadouts  if you wanted a dmr or a battle rifle  you could no longer spawn in with it but  had to scour the map to find it in its  spawn point  war zone was a brand new multiplayer  mode that makes ai enemies  alongside an opposing human team the  massive 24 player mode had teams compete  by clearing out ai enemies and bases to  earn victory points  defeating ai bosses enemies and  maintaining control of the bases would  gain victory points  however there was an additional way to  win the match if a team captured all  three bases they could attack and  destroy an enemy power core  a new rec system could be used in the  mode encouraging p